      "writtenOn": "2021-02-02T03:17:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hi Mikhail,\n\n1. IEC60958 is partially described by https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/AES3 (though there are some differences). They key reason for adding this format is to allow for fixed HDMI input patches to MSD HAL modules, without requiring patch tear-down on HDMI input audio format changes. The IEC60958 interface / format can be used to carry either PCM or an arbitrary data stream (such as compressed audio). For HDMI-in -\u003e MSD patches, the intent is for the MSD stream to be opened in IEC60958 format and for this module to process PCM or decode compressed audio as needed (IEC60958 contains a channel status block which indicates whether the payload is PCM or other compressed audio IEC61937 encapsulated data).\n\n2. Apps don\u0027t need to be aware of this audio format.\n\n3. There are a few uses of AUDIO_OUTPUT_FLAG_IEC958_NONAUDIO in the framework:\n\na) AudioTrack.cpp : the flag is added in ::set() for any track with audio format AUDIO_FORMAT_IEC61937. This seems fine, but perhaps superfluous (IEC61937 implies \"non audio\" a.k.a \"non-linear PCM\"), and AUDIO_OUTPUT_FLAG_IEC958_NONAUDIO is not a must match output flag in audio policy IOProfile.cpp.\n\nb) AudioStreamOut.cpp : the flag is added in ::open() for any stream with audio format AUDIO_FORMAT_IEC61937. It\u0027s not clear to me why the HAL needs the NONAUDIO flag if the format is IEC61937.\n\nc) SpdifStreamOut.cpp : the constructor intializes an AudioStreamOut object with AUDIO_OUTPUT_FLAG_IEC958_NONAUDIO. This is needed as the ::set() always uses PCM as the audio format, but perhaps would be easier to read / reason about if the AUDIO_OUTPUT_FLAG_IEC958_NONAUDIO flag was set in the custom config in the AudioStreamOut::open() call within SpdifStreamOut::set() just after this block as that\u0027s closer to where the logic is:\n\ncustomConfig.format \u003d AUDIO_FORMAT_PCM_16_BIT;\ncustomConfig.channel_mask \u003d AUDIO_CHANNEL_OUT_STEREO;\n\nd) AudioPolicyManager.cpp : AUDIO_OUTPUT_FLAG_IEC958_NONAUDIO is added to the MSD patch open downstream request, as a work around for lack of combined IEC61937 and raw encoded format in the openOutputStream request.\n\nIn all cases a), b), c) and d), the existence of AUDIO_FORMAT_IEC60958 can be ignored. For a HDMI input -\u003e MSD IEC60958 audio patch, a compressed audio record thread will open with that format, and a playback thread with 958 format will be open on MSD. No changes to the above classes / usage of the 958 flag should be needed.",
      "parentUuid": "ce0ebdb6_d0f77a9c",
      "revId": "75759f82f207589e552e259d0df389009119c2e7",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
